{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 c6 6. Bc4 Bf5 7. O-O e6 8. Re1 Nbd7 { Authored anchor. Re1 creates pressure on the e-file while Black is still developing. The black king and queen bishop must be coordinated before the center opens. } 9. Bd2 Qc7 10. Nh4 Bg4 { Plan: Develop ...Be7 or ...Bb4 when safe, then castle. Check whether e6 is pinned or overworked before recapturing in the center. Opponent resource: White can use Nh4 against Bf5 and d5 to open lines. Do not treat the e6 pawn as defended merely because the king stands behind it. } *

