{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 c6 6. Bd3 Bg4 7. O-O e6 { Authored anchor. Bd3 aims at h7 and supports central control. ...Bg4 develops actively against Nf3, reducing one possible supporter of e5. } 8. h3 Bh5 9. Bf4 Qd8 10. Re1 Bd6 { Plan: Develop ...Nbd7 and the king bishop, then choose king safety. If ...Bxf3 is considered, compare White's recapture and the resulting bishop pair. Opponent resource: Bxh7+ motifs depend on the king position and supporting pieces. Do not create a hook with ...h6 or ...g6 without checking the attacking consequences. } *

