{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 c6 6. Be2 Bf5 7. O-O e6 { Authored anchor. White chooses modest development instead of immediate bishop pressure on f7. Black can complete a sound formation while retaining central counterplay. } 8. Nh4 Bg6 9. g3 Be7 10. Bf3 Nbd7 { Plan: Develop ...Nbd7 and ...Be7, castle, then seek a justified pawn break. Exchanging one pair of pieces often helps the side with less space. Opponent resource: Quiet development may prepare Ne5 or Nh4. Do not drift into several queen moves just because there is no immediate attack. } *

