{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 c6 6. g3 Bf5 7. Bg2 e6 8. O-O { Authored anchor. The g2 bishop puts long-term pressure on the center and queenside. Black should develop while monitoring when the diagonal becomes open. } 8... h6 9. Ne5 Nbd7 10. Qe2 Nxe5 { Plan: Place the king bishop and knight, castle safely and contest d5. ...h6 can preserve Bf5 only if its time cost and king-safety effects are acceptable. Opponent resource: White can exchange central pawns and expose b7. A queen on a5 does not defend every queenside target. } *

