{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 Bf5 6. Ne5 c6 { Authored anchor. ...c6 controls b5 and gives the queen retreat options while White's knight occupies e5. Black must check tactical threats before chasing the knight. } 7. Bc4 e6 8. g4 Bg6 9. h4 Nbd7 10. Nxd7 Nxd7 { Plan: Develop ...e6 and ...Nbd7 when safe, or exchange the active knight if that improves coordination. Keep the queen away from discovered attacks. Opponent resource: White may play g4 against Bf5. The bishop needs a safe square and the queen may become a second tactical target. } *

