{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 Bf5 6. Ne5 c6 7. g4 Be6 { Authored anchor. Be6 saves the bishop and avoids the immediate h4 chase that can follow a retreat to g6. The engine comparison favors this retreat in the exact position shown. } 8. Bc4 Nbd7 9. Bxe6 Nxe5 10. Qe2 Ng6 { Plan: Complete development and inspect the center before counterattacking the advanced pawns. Keep the queen safe from discovered attacks as White's knight moves. Opponent resource: White still has space and can attack the bishop or queen with developing moves. A retreat solves the current threat, not the whole position. } *

[Event "SC-09 An immediate Bd2 hits the queen"]
[Site "Original study material"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
