{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. Bd2 c6 { Authored anchor. Bd2 creates a potential discovered attack along the d2-a5 diagonal when Nc3 moves. ...c6 supplies a retreat and limits Nb5. } 6. Bc4 Bf5 7. Nd5 Qd8 8. Nxf6+ exf6 9. Qe2+ Be7 10. Nf3 O-O { Plan: Watch every move of Nc3: it can reveal an attack on the queen. Develop ...Bf5 and ...e6 only after checking the queen's actual safety. Opponent resource: Nd5 or Ne4 can be both a central move and a discovered queen attack. A familiar setup does not exempt you from that calculation. } *

[Event "SC-10 The b4 pawn offer"]
[Site "Original study material"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
