[White "White study side"]
[Black "Black study side"]
[Result "*"]

{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. b4 Qxb4 { Authored anchor. Black can accept the offered pawn, but the queen now faces a series of developing attacks. This is a concrete branch that deserves calculation before practical use. } 5. Rb1 Qd6 6. Nf3 Nf6 7. d4 g6 8. Bc4 Bg7 9. O-O O-O 10. Rb3 c5 { Plan: Find safe queen squares and develop quickly. Return the extra pawn if that gets the king safe and prevents the queen being trapped. Opponent resource: Rb1, Nb5 and developing bishops may gain tempi. Counting only the extra pawn ignores the cost of the queen's excursion. } *

