{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. d4 Nf6 5. d5 { Authored anchor. The advanced d-pawn gains space and restricts Black's queen knight. Black must challenge the wedge or develop around it. } 5... c6 6. Bd2 Qc7 7. dxc6 Nxc6 8. Nf3 g6 9. Bd3 Bg7 10. O-O O-O { Plan: Examine ...c6 and the resulting dxc6 recapture. Seek active development with a clear route for the queen and the f8 bishop. Opponent resource: White can support the pawn and gain further space. A slow sequence of waiting moves may leave Black permanently cramped. } *

