{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qa5 4. Bc4 Nf6 5. d4 c6 6. Nf3 Bf5 { Authored anchor. The early bishop makes f7 pressure visible sooner, but the position can transpose to the main route after Nf3. Black should recognize the transposition without ignoring immediate checks. } 7. Ne5 e6 8. g4 Bg6 9. h4 Nbd7 10. Nxd7 Nxd7 { Plan: Develop ...e6 and ...Nbd7, checking whether a bishop or knight sacrifice on f7 has real support. Castle once the position is ready. Opponent resource: An early bishop move can combine with a fast queen move. Do not capture an apparently loose central pawn without considering checks. } *

