{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. e5 c5 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. Bb5 Bd7 { Authored anchor. White declines the central exchange and gains space. ...c5 challenges the base that White may build with d4, while ...Nc6 adds central pressure. } 5. Bxc6 Bxc6 6. d4 e6 7. Nc3 Ne7 8. Ne2 Nf5 9. a4 b5 10. axb5 Bxb5 { Plan: Develop the king side and decide whether ...e6 or ...Bg4 best fits White's setup. Attack the pawn chain rather than automatically bringing the queen out. Opponent resource: White may establish d4 and a French-like space advantage. Capturing e5 before it is safe can leave a piece pinned or a queen exposed. } *

