{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. Nc3 dxe4 3. Nxe4 Nf6 4. Nxf6+ exf6 { Authored anchor. Black exchanges the central pawn and accepts doubled f-pawns in return for development and open lines. The position has its own structure and is not a ...Qa5 line. } 5. d4 Bd6 6. Nf3 O-O 7. Be2 c5 8. Be3 cxd4 9. Nxd4 Nc6 10. c3 Qe7 { Plan: Develop the bishops actively, castle safely and consider ...c5. The bishop pair and central access can compensate for imperfect pawn shape. Opponent resource: White can target the f-pawns in an endgame. Do not exchange active bishops automatically while keeping only the structural weakness. } *

