{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. d4 dxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. f3 exf3 5. Nxf3 Bf5 { Authored anchor. White offers a pawn for development and open attacking lines. ...Bf5 develops before ...e6 and makes the extra material easier to defend. } 6. Bd3 Bxd3 7. Qxd3 c6 8. Bg5 e6 9. O-O-O Nbd7 10. Kb1 Be7 { Plan: Finish development, castle when safe and return the pawn if necessary to neutralize the initiative. Keep f7 and the central files under observation. Opponent resource: White can use Bc4, Ne5 and Qe2 against a slow defense. Greedy pawn grabbing while the king stays central is the main practical danger. } *

