{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. Nf3 dxe4 3. Ng5 Nf6 4. Nc3 Bf5 { Authored anchor. Black accepts the central pawn and develops with support for e4. White attacks quickly with knights and hopes to recover material with tempi. } 5. d3 Bg4 6. Qd2 exd3 7. Bxd3 Nc6 8. Qf4 Bh5 9. Nge4 Bg6 10. Be3 e5 { Plan: Develop ...e6 and the king bishop, checking tactical pressure on f7. If the pawn costs too much time to hold, return it for safe development. Opponent resource: Nxf7 and threats against the queen can appear. The e4 pawn is not a prize worth losing castling or a piece. } *

