{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. d4 Nf6 4. Nf3 Bg4 5. Be2 e6 { Authored anchor. White does not attack the queen immediately. Black develops the knight and bishop, keeping the queen flexible rather than committing to a retreat without a threat. } 6. h3 Bxf3 7. Bxf3 Qd6 8. O-O c6 9. g3 Nbd7 10. Re1 Rd8 { Plan: Develop ...Nc6 or ...Nbd7 according to the center and castle safely. Notice if Nc3 later gains a tempo with a discovered threat. Opponent resource: White can play c4 to chase the queen while supporting d4. Keep safe retreat squares before making a pawn commitment. } *

