{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. d4 Bg4 5. Be2 e6 6. O-O { Authored anchor. White postpones Nc3 and c4 while developing. Black can use the time to bring pieces out, but must not assume the queen can remain central forever. } 6... Nc6 7. c3 Qd8 8. h3 Bh5 9. Nbd2 Bd6 10. Ne5 Bxe5 { Plan: Complete development and answer a future c4 or Nc3 with a safe queen retreat. Compare the bishop exchange on f3 before surrendering the bishop pair. Opponent resource: A central queen can be hit by several different pieces. Do not spend the next move on an unrelated wing pawn. } *

