{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. d3 dxe4 3. dxe4 Qxd1+ 4. Kxd1 { Authored anchor. The early exchange permits a queen trade and removes White's castling rights. With queens gone, the centralized white king is less exposed than it would be in a middlegame. } 4... Nc6 5. Nd2 Nf6 6. c3 g5 7. Kc2 h5 8. h3 Bh6 9. Ngf3 Bd7 10. b4 g4 { Plan: Develop rapidly and target e4 if it is weak. Use the king-safety lead as a development opportunity rather than expecting a mating attack without queens. Opponent resource: White can consolidate with Bd3 and Ke2. Do not overestimate a lost castling right in a simplified position. } *

