{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qd8 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 c6 6. Bc4 Bf5 { Authored anchor. Returning the queen avoids repeated queen attacks but concedes a clear developing tempo. This is an optional alternative, not a move to mix into an existing ...Qa5 position. } 7. Ne5 e6 8. g4 Bg6 9. h4 Nbd7 10. Qe2 Bb4 { Plan: Build ...e6 and ...Nbd7, develop the bishop and castle. Seek central counterplay before White converts extra space into a sustained attack. Opponent resource: White can use Ne5 or d5 while Black is still developing. The queen's safety alone does not solve the space problem. } *

