{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qd6 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 a6 { Authored anchor. The queen on d6 supports the center but can be targeted by Ne4, Bf4 or later central moves. ...a6 keeps Nb5 under control. } 6. g3 Bg4 7. h3 Bxf3 8. Qxf3 c6 9. Be3 e6 10. O-O-O Nd5 { Plan: Develop with a clear plan for ...b5 or ...Nc6 when appropriate. Decide on the queen bishop before fixing the e-pawn. Opponent resource: Every pawn tempo delays king safety. White can build pressure quickly if the queen and king both remain exposed. } *

