{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Nxd5 4. Nf3 g6 5. Be2 Bg7 6. O-O O-O { Authored anchor. Black delays recapturing and then uses the knight. The fianchetto creates a different repertoire from the queen-recapture Scandinavian. } 7. c4 Nb6 8. Nc3 Bg4 9. h3 Bxf3 10. Bxf3 c6 { Plan: Develop the queen knight and challenge d4 with ...c5. Keep the d5 knight safe from c4 and central exchanges. Opponent resource: White may gain tempi with c4. A knight recapture avoids queen attacks but does not eliminate attacks on the recapturing piece. } *

