{ Original Scandinavian Defense course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. c4 c6 4. dxc6 Nxc6 5. d4 e5 { Authored anchor. Black offers a second pawn to gain development and central activity. This is an optional gambit branch requiring exact calculation, not part of the main ...Qa5 course repertoire. } 6. d5 Bc5 7. Be3 Nd4 8. Nf3 O-O 9. Nxd4 exd4 10. Bxd4 Bg4 { Plan: Develop actively and look for central pressure rather than trying to regain the pawn with slow moves. Compare this risk with the direct queen-recapture repertoire. Opponent resource: White can consolidate extra material. A gambit is not justified by development alone if no concrete pressure follows. } *

